The thing is that the game *doesn't* specify that "tripe rations" are prepared
specifically for animals- unlike, say, a MilkBone.  It says that tripe is dog
food; so that particular bias is built into Nethack.

I agree that the YANI, by calling tripe "menudo" (as opposed to "busecca", for
example) flirts with condescension.  (In its defense, menudo is the way of
preparing tripe that Americans, at least, are most likely to be familiar
with.)[1] But I'd hesitate before calling it racist.[2]

